item.description:
arXiv:2609.21657v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: Let $\mu$ be a positive Borel measure on $[0,1)$ and $\omega$ a radial weight. In this paper we consider the Ces\`aro-type operator $C_{\mu,\omega}$ induced by the reproducing kernel $B^{\omega}$ of the weighted Bergman space $A^2_{\omega}$, given by $$ C_{\mu,\omega}(f)(z)=\int_{0}^{1}f(tz)B^{\omega}_t(z)\,d\mu(t), \quad z \in \mathbb{D}, $$ for functions $f$ analytic in $\mathbb{D}$. Under the assumption that $\omega$ satisfies a natural doubling property, we study the boundedness of $C_{\mu,\omega}$ acting on several spaces of analytic functions, including Hardy spaces $H^p$ and weighted Bergman spaces $A^p_{
u}$. For $0<p,q<\infty$ and a two-sided doubling weight $
u$, we completely characterize when $C_{\mu,\omega}: H^p 	o H^q$ and $C_{\mu,\omega}: A^p_{
u} 	o A^q_{
u}$ are bounded in terms of the interplay of tail integrals or moments of the inducing weights and the measure $\mu$. Many of the results obtained are new even in the setting of standard weights or when the Bergman reproducing kernel is replaced by the Cauchy kernel. In addition, we consider $C_{\mu,\omega}$ acting on $H^{\infty}$, Korenblum spaces and weighted Hardy spaces.
